In article <1991Jan28.182421.25008@digibd.com> merlyn@digibd.com (Brian Westley (Merlyn LeRoy)) writes:
>Scroll of duplication

Interesting.  Don't think cursed things should be destroyed, though.  A
cursed scroll of duplication could destroy the thing being duplicated,
though.  Blessed could duplicate as many as you have in your pack,
while uncursed would duplicate only one, i.e., 2 potions of holy water
could become 4 with a blessed scroll of duplication, but only 3 with 
an uncursed.

>Wand of clone monster

Too easy to abuse.  This is hard enough to balance in a game like Moria,
in a game like NetHack, which is hardly balanced in the first place, it
would throw things way out of whack.

>Wand of everything

Good idea.  Wonder what engraving with it would do?

>Wand of fireballs

Fine.  Caster would have to be damaged if he was in the ball, of course.
Would it destroy scrolls and potions laying on the ground in the affected
area?

